The [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls #4471 one issue with one fix queued. It holds two
bugs. The desk merges on subject lines, and subject lines cannot tell these two apart.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued fix changes the parser. It does not change the hint on the booking-v3 form, so the
hint reports keep coming after the fix ships.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

## The parser bug

The shared parser reads every date month first, so a day-first tenant's dates come out flipped:
7 April becomes 4 July. It reaches every tenant on file, through the app, through email, and
through the booking-v2 form. This is the bug the queued fix is for.

## The hint bug

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at a day-first tenant type
what the hint says, month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. It reaches only
reports that come through the form at a tenant on booking-v3. The same tenants' app and email
reports belong to the parser bug.

The fix is a different one: the form's hint has to match the order the form reads.

## How to tell them apart

Use `causeOf` in `causes.ts`. It looks at the tenant's locale, the tenant's form and the channel.

- **Not the subject.** Every subject on a hint report also appears on parser reports.
- **Not the intake tag.** Intake guesses from the reporter's browser. The "tagged as" column shows
  how often that guess disagrees with the cause.
- **Not the raw export.** Its pages overlap and some reports come twice. The table counts each id
  once.

## Reports that do not read as a flip

The note under the table counts reports the desk read as a one-day move. The kb files a report by
its tenant, so they count under the parser bug. A month-first parser cannot move 12 May to 11 May,
though, and R-41344 says clients in Lisbon and Toronto got different days for one meeting. That
points at time zones. Nobody has checked it. If engineering finds another cause, they move out of
the parser count and get their own ticket.

## Still open

- The incident page still says one issue. Its owner has to update it.
- Decision 0001 still tells the desk to merge on subject. A decision is never edited, so a new
  record has to replace it, and the triage page has to follow.

